Appearance becomes a real setting, and the colour control becomes usable
===========================================================================

Three faults, one shape: the interface kept its own copy of something the application owns.

1. The theme lived only in localStorage. The backend has an AppPreferences service with
   getPreferences / setPreference — and the value it held was never written to disk, so it was not a
   setting either. Preferences are now read at boot from <data_dir>/preferences.json and written back
   when the interface changes one; localStorage stays as the paint cache so the window comes up in the
   right theme instead of flashing the default while the bridge answers.

2. The custom theme used <input type="color">. WebKitGTK renders that as a palette grid that COMMITS
   ON FIRST TOUCH: no dragging a dial, no looking at it, no adjusting again and then accepting — the
   first nudge is the result. It also has no saturation control, so a neon green is unreachable.
   Replaced with hue / saturation / lightness sliders, a hex field and a live swatch. The sliders are
   authoritative while you drag: deriving HSL back out of the 8-bit hex on every step drifts (hue 135,
   saturation 100, lightness 50 lands on #00ff3c after a few nudges instead of #00ff41), and rounding
   hue to whole degrees turns a typed #00ff41 into #00ff40. Hue keeps its fraction; the hex re-seeds
   the sliders only when you type in it.

   Verified by driving the real function in a browser: typed #00ff41, #7fff00, #39ff14, #ffffff and
   #000000 all round-trip to themselves with the sliders landing on 135/100/50, 90/100/50, 111/100/54,
   0/0/100, 0/0/0; a slow drag up through saturation and down through hue is reversible with no
   creep; full saturation at hue 135 yields #00ff40, one step off the ideal only because a five-degree
   step cannot land on 135.29. Writes behind a drag settle for 200 ms instead of one file write each.

3. Matrix, Amber and Ice were tinted rather than phosphor. Matrix was #00ff88 on #7dffa8 — mint, not
   the green anybody means by Matrix. Now #00ff41 on #8dff9f over #000800; amber #ffb000 over
   #0a0600; ice #00e5ff over #000a0f. The swatches in the picker describe the same values they claim.

   Verified in a browser: body background and text follow each theme (rgb(0,8,0) / rgb(141,255,159)
   matrix, rgb(10,6,0) / rgb(255,198,92) amber, rgb(0,10,15) / rgb(168,236,255) ice).

